{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 10: the truck fleet as a six-stage ageing chain (two years per class). With more classes, retirements bunch near the average life of 12 years, and the echo of the first purchase lasts longer. }
Class Time=
	2
	~	year
	~	Average years in each age class.
	|
Trucks Class 1= INTEG(
	Purchases - Ageing 1,
	300)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks of about 0 to 2 years.
	|
Ageing 1=
	Trucks Class 1 / Class Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Cost Class 1=
	1
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	|
Trucks Class 2= INTEG(
	Ageing 1 - Ageing 2,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks of about 2 to 4 years.
	|
Ageing 2=
	Trucks Class 2 / Class Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Cost Class 2=
	3
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	|
Trucks Class 3= INTEG(
	Ageing 2 - Ageing 3,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks of about 4 to 6 years.
	|
Ageing 3=
	Trucks Class 3 / Class Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Cost Class 3=
	5
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	|
Trucks Class 4= INTEG(
	Ageing 3 - Ageing 4,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks of about 6 to 8 years.
	|
Ageing 4=
	Trucks Class 4 / Class Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Cost Class 4=
	8
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	|
Trucks Class 5= INTEG(
	Ageing 4 - Ageing 5,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks of about 8 to 10 years.
	|
Ageing 5=
	Trucks Class 5 / Class Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Cost Class 5=
	12
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	|
Trucks Class 6= INTEG(
	Ageing 5 - Retirements,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks of about 10 to 12 years.
	|
Retirements=
	Trucks Class 6 / Class Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Cost Class 6=
	16
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	|
Purchases=
	Retirements
	~	truck/year
	~	Every retired truck is replaced at once.
	|
Maintenance Cost=
	Cost Class 1 * Trucks Class 1 + Cost Class 2 * Trucks Class 2 + Cost Class 3 * Trucks Class 3 + Cost Class 4 * Trucks Class 4 + Cost Class 5 * Trucks Class 5 + Cost Class 6 * Trucks Class 6
	~	kUSD/year
	~	|
Fleet=
	Trucks Class 1 + Trucks Class 2 + Trucks Class 3 + Trucks Class 4 + Trucks Class 5 + Trucks Class 6
	~	truck
	~	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ year ~ |
FINAL TIME = 60 ~ year ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ year ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ year ~ |
